    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "co2_thermal_conductivity_info",
      "content": "## Thermal Conductivity Units Conversion\n\n**Common Conversions:**\n- 1 W/(m·K) = 0.5779 Btu(IT)/(ft·h·°F) = 0.04815 Btu(IT)/(in·h·°F) = 0.85984 kcal/(m·h·°C)\n- 1 Btu(IT)/(ft·h·°F) = 1.731 W/(m·K)\n- 1 kcal/(m·h·°C) = 1.163 W/(m·K)\n\n**Notes:**\n- Thermal conductivity is the ability of a material to conduct heat\n- Units: W/(m·K) in SI system, Btu/(h·ft·°F) in Imperial system, mW/(m·K), kcal(IT)/(h·m·K), Btu(IT)/(h·ft·°F), (Btu(IT)·in)/(h·ft²·°F)\n- Data provided for various states: Gas, Liquid, and Supercritical phase\n- Measurements at different pressures: 0.1, 1, 5, 10, 100, and 1000 bara"
